{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Both registered questions were already settled and recorded, so I opened one independent lead on the safety side and submitted its probe. Because the captured suites drop messages but deliver them in order, while the core's Recover path exists precisely for out-of-order replication, the new question asks whether a follower that misses an `AcceptDecide` and then receives a later one first still ends with the leader's decided values and keeps progressing. The probe drives three real `OmniPaxos` instances directly, captures the `AcceptDecide` carrying entry 4, delivers the one for entry 5 (the sequence break), then delivers the held message late, and compares each node's decided values; locally the control and the reordered case each ended with entries 1–6 decided on all three nodes and the follower equal to the leader, so the submitted execution is framed as a bounded negative with the receipt as its evidence. Incomplete: that receipt is pending, and the probe observes endpoints only — it does not sample which intermediate phase the follower passed through.\"}"}}
